umi-mainline - running mainline Linux on the Xiaomi Mi 10 (SM8250 / "umi")

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only

This repository deliberately mixes four kinds of material, each under the
license that matches how it has to be used.  The full text of every license
referenced here is in LICENSES/.

    patches/**/*.c              GPL-2.0-only   (LICENSES/GPL-2.0-only.txt)
        Kernel drivers.  Not negotiable: a driver cannot enter the Linux
        kernel under anything else.

    dts/**/*.dts, dts/**/*.dtsi BSD-3-Clause   (LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause.txt)
        Device trees.  Same license as the arm64 Qualcomm device trees that
        already live upstream, so these files can be picked up by the kernel
        tree without any relicensing step.

    scripts/**, tools/**        CC0-1.0        (LICENSES/CC0-1.0.txt)
        Build scripts and host-side helpers.  Public domain dedication:
        copy them, change them, relicence them, no attribution required.

    docs/**, README.md          CC-BY-4.0      (LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt)
        Written documentation.  Reuse and translate freely, keep the
        attribution.

Unless a file says otherwise, the license above applies to it; a
SPDX-License-Identifier: tag always wins over this table.

Third-party material used as reference while porting (vendor kernel sources,
vendor device trees, firmware images) is NOT covered by the licenses above and
is not redistributed here.  See "Third-party material" in README.md.